      "last_decision": {
        "at": "2026-10-19T16:31:19.071437+00:00",
        "symbol": "AMZN",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "Third consecutive hold, still flat AMZN.NAS into the Oct 29 Q3 print. The fresh quote 262.86/262.91 versus 262.84/262.89 at the prior decision is a de minimis pricing event and resolves no economic objection. No primary filing with AWS segment margin, 2026 capex total, FCF reconciliation or Anthropic facility draw status has arrived; the day's catalyst remains publisher-reported sell-side opinion (Morgan Stanley top-pick, target $350). This packet does newly reconcile the debt discrepancy: the as-filed Q2-2026 balance sheet shows long-term debt $65,648M to $128,894M with $81,925M of H1 long-term debt proceeds, confirming a leverage-extended build rather than settling the contested interpretation. Entering now still means paying up for a single-broker pop into a binary, mark-heavy print at ~24% annualized volatility. Hold and re-present with primary Q3 disclosure.",
        "thesis": "Watch thesis unchanged since the prior two holds. Filing-verified facts stand: Q2 2026 net income $62,647M rests on $53,381M of non-operating income, dominated by $50.5B upward private-company (Anthropic preferred) marks; TTM FCF is -$7,604M on $161,403M OCF against $169,007M net capex; the 10-Q balance sheet shows long-term debt rising from $65,648M to $128,894M in six months with $81,925M of proceeds; AWS performance obligations ~$496B including >$100B each OpenAI and Anthropic expansions tied to AWS chip performance, while Amazon commits up to a $20B facility to Anthropic. Macro: DGS10 5.10%, DGS30 5.43% discount-rate headwind; VIX 16.46, BBB 1.05%, HY 3.23% keep near-term funding benign. The contested question - backlog-backed investment phase versus circular leverage - is undecidable without the Oct 29 segment disclosure. The Morgan Stanley note is one syndicated broker vote, not disclosure; the $350 target is a hypothesis. Full-document certification remains unimplemented and is disclosed; per standing demo authorization that alone does not veto, but entry still waits on primary segment data.",
        "countercase": "Waiting forfeits upside: the Morgan Stanley top-pick cites AWS acceleration and expanding retail margins via AI/robotics, and a Wedgewood Q3 letter praises AWS margin expansion; if the print verifies AWS growth with expanding segment margin, capex near the $53.1B/quarter H1 pace and trailing FCF turning positive, the re-rating gaps 8-12% overnight without me. Tight spreads make the new debt genuinely cheap today, the $496B backlog exceeds three years of AWS-scale demand, and the 200-session mean (242.7) sits ~7% below the quote, implying the uptrend is intact. The X-Energy/AEP nuclear evaluation is long-dated energy optionality. Meta's Wednesday capex commentary could also reset sector sentiment favorably rather than adversely.",
        "invalidation": "Buy trigger (thesis resolution, not change): the Oct 29 Q3 print verifies AWS segment revenue growth and operating margin, a concrete 2026 capex total versus the $128.3B FY2025 base, and trailing FCF against the negative TTM -$7.6B run-rate - enter only then at 0.5% strategy risk with the computed 2-ATR broker stop. Abort triggers: a primary filing showing capex guidance materially above cash generation with no contracted-demand offset; AWS deceleration; an Anthropic mark reversal or facility drawdown evidencing circular-financing deterioration; HY spreads widening past ~3.6% with a further 10-year rise; or a close below the 200-session mean (~243 USD equivalent) on above-average volume, voiding the setup.",
